cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or source data, please cite this software and the associated manuscript."
title: "Article-grouped and post-cutoff evaluation reveals limits of parameter-efficient adaptation in scientific visual question answering"
version: 1.1.0
type: software
abstract: "Reproducibility code and aggregate source data for parameter-efficient option-shared residual adaptation over frozen CLIP and BiomedCLIP representations on PMC-VQA, including article-grouped validation, leakage-free data scaling, post-cutoff temporal evaluation, an end-to-end efficiency audit, and an image-correspondence shuffle control."
